review_comments:
When all of the following are true:
 - the resulting index is the same as the input index;
 - `group_keys` is left unspecified in the call to `.groupby(...)`;
 - the function is not in transformation_kernels (e.g. `cumsum` or `shift`); and
 - the result is either not computed by `_python_agg_general` or is nonempty.

I am wondering if instead of the last bullet, we should just not warn/override on any empty result. Will investigate.

